    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure rule for membership level 4 in `Owner.getMembershipLevel()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`).\n\n**The change:**\n- The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for an email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are now capped at 3 first.\n- A new tenure factor grants +1 (reaching level 4) only when the owner's tenure \u2014 `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now())` \u2014 is **more than 365 days**.\n- The overall result is capped at 4.\n- Added the `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` import and updated the Javadoc.\n\nBecause a newly created owner has `registrationDate` set to today, its tenure is 0 days (not > 365), so it never gets the 4th increment. A new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` of 0 lands at level 3, exactly as the spec and the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test require.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit log line confirms the new owner is created at `membershipLevel=3`.",
